# Findings accepted as known risk, not fixed — see justification for each.
# This project is dev-only with no production traffic yet (see CLAUDE.md
# §8, "Estratégia de branch"); several hardening measures here trade real
# cost/complexity for protecting an environment nothing depends on today.
# Revisit each when its own trigger below is met — do not blanket-remove
# this file just because Trivy started passing.

# AWS-0011: CloudFront distribution has no WAF.
# Already a deliberate, documented backlog decision (CLAUDE.md §10 item 18):
# "WAF no Admin CloudFront — quando houver tráfego real". Same reasoning
# extends to the frontend distribution, which this rule also flags.
AVD-AWS-0011

# AWS-0015: CloudTrail doesn't use a customer-managed KMS key.
# AWS-0132: S3 bucket doesn't use a customer-managed KMS key.
# Both require creating and managing a real KMS CMK (~$1/month + per-request
# cost, plus a key policy to maintain) to protect logs of a dev environment
# with no real user data. Trigger to revisit: production environment exists,
# or CloudTrail/S3 here start holding data with real confidentiality needs.
AVD-AWS-0015
AVD-AWS-0132
